	chapter.7607345A1BF3481B.title: "&6&l⚡ Legends"
	quest.004011C7AA12F1C1.quest_desc: "Cook this in a furnace to use it"
	quest.01F1C546339F7BC2.quest_desc: [
		"When looking for a good trade, you always have to remove the villagers workstation, in order to reset their trades. The trade cycle button solves this problem. If a villager hasn't been traded before, you can just press it and the trades reset automatically."
		""
		"Alternatively you can use the C (by default) key to cycle trades."
		""
		"This also works for normal villagers."
	]
	quest.046BE86EF3A8ADC2.quest_desc: [
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Ahhh yes — the medical side of Pokémon!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"You’ve come to the right—wait, no, the wrong—wait, no no, definitely the right place! Haha… silly me. Classic me."
		""
		"Anyway! Behold:"
		""
		"Potions!"
		""
		"Revives!"
		""
		"Other potions that I definitely didn’t find already opened!"
		""
		"Some of them looked a bit… off, so I poured them into different bottles to keep track. Totally fine. Totally safe."
		"Probably."
		""
		"Each one does something helpful. I think."
		"Color-coded, mostly. Smells weird, but that’s the healing, you know?"
		""
		"So! You want to fix your team or take a gamble on mystery medicine?"
		"I’ve got both."
	]
	quest.046BE86EF3A8ADC2.title: "Medical"
	quest.051D10351C808F2D.quest_desc: "\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Iron Meshes—now we’re getting somewhere. The better the mesh, the better the drops, with Netherite being the best of the bunch. Some meshes work better with certain materials than others, so make sure to use JEI to check what you can get. Just press ‘U’ on the mesh to see its potential drops."
	quest.05721132460CE1A5.quest_desc: [
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Ah, feast your eyes on these pointy-type gems!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"I think they're gems. Not entirely sure, really — but the colors are vibrant, and that’s what matters, right? Match nicely if you squint."
		""
		"Now, this one here — shaped a bit like coal? Yeah, that’s a coal-type gem, very rare… probably."
		"And these cracked ones? That’s not damage, no no — that’s called personality. Makes ’em unique. Distressed look. Very in right now."
		""
		"They’re pretty good, I promise. Probably."
	]
	quest.05721132460CE1A5.title: "Pointy Gems"
	quest.087F9C40B4545AE5.quest_desc: "This is used to craft meshes, with the String Mesh being the first available. I recommend starting with a 3x3 sieve setup, but you can go bigger or smaller—it's completely up to you"
	quest.0945B6E883E32A90.quest_desc: "By sieving dirt, you can obtain every color you’re looking for."
	quest.0AB80C0705795BE0.title: "Epic"
	quest.0AC803ACD9A7FF2A.quest_desc: "\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Silkworms infest leaves, and once the infestation spreads, breaking the leaves with your crook will yield string. String is vital for progression, so don’t skip this step. Luckily, these little worms work fast—so you won’t be stuck waiting for long."
	quest.0D641C9CF1E1D7D4.quest_desc: "Eventually, you’ll get a chest with some saplings. You can always get more, so don’t stress—this is just the beginning."
	quest.0ED64547FC4F72EE.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to my Cobblemon One Block!"
		"This is a mostly vanilla-plus experience, where everything is accessible through sifting. However, there are also gyms, which you can challenge using the Radical Trainers mod—either through the Shiny Pearl or Radical Red storylines."
		""
		"I highly recommend trying this, as it adds a competitive edge along with a true Cobblemon sense of progression."
		""
		"The One Block is the standard One Block experience, so make the most of every stage. As you may know, they don’t stick around for very long! But don’t worry—thanks to additional mods, everything remains accessible as you progress."
		""
		"Enjoy your journey, and good luck becoming the ultimate trainer!"
	]
	quest.0ED64547FC4F72EE.title: "Information"
	quest.0F9CA8C190C4EB0D.quest_desc: [
		"This mod is packed with content — so much that it now includes every battle gimmick from the Pokémon series, each with its own unique mechanics and methods of unlocking."
		""
		"✅ Mega Evolutions"
		"Includes all 48 Mega Evolutions"
		""
		"Can be configured to only allow battling Megas (not using them)"
		""
		"Cosmetic customization for Mega Bracelets"
		""
		"Emissive textures for a more dynamic visual effect"
		""
		"Full stat and ability changes when a Pokémon Mega Evolves"
		""
		"Riding support for Megas"
		""
		"Curios/Trinkets compatibility for added customization"
		""
		"✅ Other Major Gimmicks Included"
		"Primal Reversions (Groudon and Kyogre)"
		""
		"Z-Moves system fully integrated"
		""
		"Dynamaxing and Gigantamaxing supported"
		""
		"Tera Types added with full mechanics"
		""
		"Ultra Burst (Necrozma transformation mechanic)"
		""
		"Ultra Necrozma included"
		""
		"All fusion Pokémon (like Kyurem, Calyrex forms, etc.)"
		""
		"Additional Notes:"
		"Each gimmick has its own method of unlocking, encouraging exploration and variety."
		""
		"The mod supports various playstyles and configs, so you can tailor the experience to how challenging or immersive you want it to be."
		""
		"With so many features, this mod massively expands your gameplay options — perfect for players looking for a deep, competitive, and content-rich experience."
	]
	quest.0F9CA8C190C4EB0D.title: "MegaShowDown"
	quest.107DB8EA17121663.quest_desc: [
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Candy shop? Caaandy shop? I think that’s a song... maybe. Doesn’t matter.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"What does matter is — I got sweets. Special sweets. Rare. Exotic. Probably magical. Possibly expired. Who can say?"
		""
		"Some of these might even be safe for Pokémon! Or... not."
		"Check the packaging before you give it to one, yeah? I’m like... 55% sure it’s fine. Solid odds, really."
		""
		"So — want some? They’re sugary. They’re mysterious."
		"They’re definitely candy. Probably."
	]
	quest.107DB8EA17121663.title: "Candy Shop Candy Shop"
	quest.12417572054691BE.quest_desc: [
		"Shinies – We All Love Them!"
		""
		"Shinies are a fan favorite, but they can be incredibly difficult to find. So, in this modpack, I've decided to introduce a fun twist: every \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bioring Monday,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" shiny odds will be boosted to twice the normal rate!"
		""
		"The base shiny odds have also been adjusted from the original 1 in 8192 to 1 in 4096, making them more reasonable overall. This change is meant to make shiny hunting more enjoyable without removing the challenge entirely."
		""
		"Why the change? The old odds were just too high, and I personally prefer a slightly more generous system. Happy hunting, and may your Mondays be extra shiny!"
	]
	quest.12E5930AE01189AE.quest_desc: "Cook this in a furnace to use it"
