	]
	quest.1FF0E8E09400F3E6.quest_subtitle: "&7Lake Guardian"
	quest.1FF0E8E09400F3E6.title: "&d&lMesprit"
	quest.211EB27D64636694.quest_desc: [
		"The three beasts of Johto never stop running."
		""
		"&7Only an absurd treasure makes one of them stop and look at you."
		""
		"&e&lIt will appear next to you.&r &7Do not let it flee."
	]
	quest.211EB27D64636694.quest_subtitle: "&7Legendary Beast"
	quest.211EB27D64636694.title: "&e&lSuicune"
	quest.220EA0B486F33931.quest_desc: "This is an extra-strong crook—and that’s pretty much it. It works just like a regular crook, but lasts longer and helps you gather even more efficiently."
	quest.2BE905EFBD5E7D7F.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, dirt is really important."
		"However, it can be pretty grindy to get. To help with that, combining dirt with two cobblestone will give you 4 dirt in return. That means there's now a technically renewable way to get dirt — well, as long as you’ve got enough cobblestone."
	]
	quest.32117ADBFD9B230A.quest_desc: "Flint Meshes—now these are the real deal. When used with gravel, they can yield your first real materials like iron, diamonds, emeralds, and more. However, the drop rates aren’t great, so once you get some iron, it’s a smart move to upgrade your meshes for better efficiency."
	quest.342561E11FD23964.quest_desc: [
		"Knowledge, emotion and willpower."
		""
		"&7They only show up for someone who already registered everything."
		""
		"&e&lIt will appear next to you.&r"
	]
	quest.342561E11FD23964.quest_subtitle: "&7Lake Guardian"
	quest.342561E11FD23964.title: "&d&lUxie"
	quest.342B3DD82822DC35.quest_desc: "The trader block allows trading with the villager without having to deal with securing the villager. This block also allows the villager to restock in non-working hours. The restocking time of the villager is not dependent on any external sources like day/night time or dimension."
	quest.35C6DD81DA6D9754.quest_desc: [
		"This mod can definitely be a bit confusing at first, but once you get the hang of it, it’s not too hard to follow."
		""
		"To get started, you’ll need to wait for the wandering villager from the mod to spawn — that’s how you choose your storyline. You can pick between Radical Red and Shining Pearl, but I recommend going with Radical Red for the most competitive and challenging experience."
		""
		"You’ll earn badges as you progress, and these are essential for advancing through the mod. There’s also a level cap system, so make sure not to catch or level up any Pokémon above the current cap — it starts at Level 15 for the first gym leader."
		""
		"In the Radical Red path, your first gym leader is Brock, so be prepared! This mod doesn't go easy on you — expect a real challenge."
		""
		"If you ever get stuck or need more info, check the in-game Trainer Card or head over to the mod’s wiki — both are great sources of up-to-date guidance."
	]
	quest.35C6DD81DA6D9754.title: "StoryMode"
	quest.3616507498A925D8.quest_desc: [
		"In time, you’ll come across a chest containing a few saplings. Don’t worry—you can always collect more as you go. This is just the beginning of your journey, so take your time and enjoy the process."
		"Place it next to the chests to connect with the crafting table—think of it as a small starter storage system to help you stay organized"
	]
	quest.3783BECAA085F10B.quest_desc: [
		"One Block Phases Overview"
		"The One Block experience is broken into multiple phases, each with its own unique theme and resources. Here's the full list:"
		""
		"Phase 0: Tutorial"
		""
		"Phase 1: The Plains"
		""
		"Phase 2: The Underground"
		""
		"Phase 3: Icy Tundra"
		""
		"Phase 4: Steaminess (New)"
		""
		"Phase 5: Ocean"
		""
		"Phase 6: Jungle Dungeon"
		""
		"Phase 7: Red Desert"
		""
		"Phase 8: The Nether"
		""
		"Phase 9: Idyll"
		""
		"Phase 10: Travel (New)"
		""
		"Phase 11: Desolate Land"
		""
		"Phase 12: Subterranean Depths (New)"
		""
		"Phase 13: The End"
		""
		"Don’t worry — after Phase 13, there is an \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"after phase\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", meaning the experience becomes endless, so you can keep playing beyond the final listed stage."
		""
		"Important Notes:"
		"Phases Do Not Repeat: Once you move past a phase, you can’t go back to it. Be sure to gather any resources you need before advancing to the next phase."
		""
		"Don’t Rely Solely on the One Block: While it’s your main source of materials, you’ll need to explore and use other methods to obtain what you need."
		""
		"Cobblmon Spawning:"
		"Cobblmon spawn naturally on their appropriate blocks and in their natural biomes. For the best spawn rates:"
		""
		"Build a large grass platform (especially early on)."
		""
		"Don’t expect every Cobblmon to spawn from the one block itself — biomes still matter."
		""
		"Finding Biomes:"
		"You’ll still need to explore to locate different biomes. To make this easier:"
		""
		"Use the Nature’s Compass mod to find specific biomes more efficiently."
		""
		"Consider building natural environments (e.g. swamps, jungles, oceans) around your base to encourage the Cobblmon you’re looking for to spawn."
	]
	quest.3783BECAA085F10B.title: "OneBlock"
	quest.3C3C023DAD1FF329.quest_desc: "The breeder block produces baby villagers by putting in food. This also helps to reduce lag, save space and also a lot of frustration."
	quest.4168EAD004426260.title: "Common"
	quest.43CA08A75364B9F9.title: "Uncommon"
	quest.448D53BFFEEFF4F4.quest_desc: "Crooks are used to collect silkworms from leaves. Be sure to use Ultimine with them to save yourself some time and effort"
	quest.4700D36B0416F9DA.quest_desc: "You’ll need this to collect water and make dirt. Use organics to create dirt, then leave it out in the rain to collect water. Once it's filled, use a bucket to gather it."
	quest.481CF947907E8B60.quest_desc: [
		"You can dig up pebbles by Shift + Right-Clicking on the ground with an empty hand."
		""
		"From Dirt or Grass, you can find pebbles of:"
		""
		"Andesite"
		""
		"Calcite"
		""
		"Deepslate"
		""
		"Diorite"
		""
		"Dripstone"
		""
		"Granite"
		""
		"Stone"
		""
		"Tuff"
		""
		"From Netherrack, you can find pebbles of:"
		""
		"Netherrack"
		""
		"Basalt"
		""
		"Blackstone"
	]
	quest.481CF947907E8B60.title: "Pebbles"
	quest.4A0966DEC1089B5E.quest_desc: [
		"The three beasts of Johto never stop running."
		""
		"&7Only an absurd treasure makes one of them stop and look at you."
		""
		"&e&lIt will appear next to you.&r &7Do not let it flee."
	]
	quest.4A0966DEC1089B5E.quest_subtitle: "&7Legendary Beast"
	quest.4A0966DEC1089B5E.title: "&e&lEntei"
	quest.4A1C17F349C72415.quest_desc: "Ah yes, the Oak Sieve—back again. If you’ve used this mod before, you probably know what’s coming. But if not, here’s the deal: this block lets you sift materials through it, giving you a chance to obtain useful resources. In this case, it’ll help you gather most of the cobblestone-based items you'll need to move forward."
	quest.529341319CA7AF2F.quest_desc: "The iron farm block contains a complete iron farm in a single block. It produces one iron golem every four minutes. This averages about one iron ingot per minute."
	quest.54288F6026AB4C34.quest_desc: [
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Oho! What's this...?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"Look at these shiny stones! Aren’t they glorious? So shiny. All of them. Every last one."
		"...Just, uh—don’t look too closely. Best to admire from a distance, yeah?"
	]
	quest.54288F6026AB4C34.title: "Rare Shiny Rocks"
	quest.550BC38EA1D44C2B.quest_desc: [
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Ahhh, hello there, traveler...\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"Most folks call me a trader — but I prefer the term entrepreneur, personally. Has a nicer ring to it, don't you think?"
		""
		"Now then, let's get to business. You see, I have a bit of an obsession... relic coins. Glorious, shiny, ancient things! I love them. I need them. And lucky you — I've got wares. Strange wares. Rare wares. Magical? Maybe. Cursed? Who's to say."
		""
		"You can spend your precious relic coins right here. But fair warning:"
		"You're not guaranteed to get what you want."
		"You might get something completely different."
		"You might get nothing at all."
		""
		"No refunds. No complaints. No backsies."
		"Deal with it."
		""
		"Now then... care to try your luck?"
	]
	quest.550BC38EA1D44C2B.title: "Who is this..."
	quest.561833E63459CDFC.quest_desc: "You can use hammers to crush blocks into other materials—for example, cobblestone into gravel, gravel into sand, and sand into dust. The better the hammer, the longer it will last."
	quest.56194F5EEDAE9181.quest_desc: "The converter block converts villagers to zombie villagers and cures them afterwards, enabling the player that placed the block better trades from the cured villager. This block needs a golden apple, any type of potion of weakness and the villager to convert. This process takes approximately five minutes."
	quest.59A3081002F16C28.quest_desc: [
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Ahhh, hello hello! You've stumbled upon my Useful Blocks section!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"Blocks! Yes, blocks — very helpful. Very... blocky. You get it."
		""
		"Anyyyywayyy, moving on:"
		"Here’s what I’ve got for you today:"
		""
		"A Healer — zap! Your team, good as new."
		""
		"A PC — store your precious creatures in the digital void. Safe-ish."
		""
		"Some fossil stuff — bones, rocks, ancient mystery. Very science."
		""
		"Gimmighoul-related oddities — rattly, spooky, mildly cursed."
		""
		"...And a grave."
		"We don’t talk about the grave. Seriously."
		"Don’t touch it. Don’t ask. Just... don’t."
		""
		"So! Interested in some delightfully useful, slightly ominous blocks?"
	]
	quest.59A3081002F16C28.title: "Helpfull Old Blocks"
	quest.5DED4197DB2EEBBC.quest_desc: [
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Ahhh yes, seeds and... other things!\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"One of each — only one. Why? Because they’re that rare. Scarce. Precious. Legendary, even. I’ve got a few red ones too — and those? Those are the rarest of the rare."
		"Trust me."
		"Or... trust the guy who told me. Either way, very exclusive stuff."
		""
		"Now over here, I’ve got these seeds — never grown a thing in their life. Cabbage and wheat, apparently. Never heard of ‘em."
		"I live on a strict lettuce-and-water diet, myself. Keeps the soul light."
		""
		"But yeah — real nature stuff. Totally eco-friendly."
		"I’m basically saving the planet. You’re welcome."
	]
	quest.5DED4197DB2EEBBC.title: "Seeds And Stuff"
	quest.5EB36B3477BC9C64.quest_desc: [
		"Ah, yes... these dusty little bone things—\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		"Er, I mean... archaeological masterpieces from a bygone age! Yes, yes, very rare, very historical. Found them buried deep in the earth — or maybe just under my rug, who knows?"
		""
		"Anyway... want one? They’re cheap. Practically giving them away."
		"(But don’t ask too many questions.)"
	]
	quest.5EB36B3477BC9C64.title: "Dusty Rocks I think...."
	quest.5EEB370876DD0819.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe creator.&r"
		""
		"&cRequires all five mythicals: Mew, Celebi, Jirachi, Victini and Manaphy.&r"
		"There is nothing left in this game that you have not done."
		""
		"&e&lIt will appear next to you.&r &7One shot. Do not miss."
	]
	quest.5EEB370876DD0819.quest_subtitle: "&7The one who made it all"
	quest.5EEB370876DD0819.title: "&6&l&nARCEUS"
	quest.615946DE5C423DC0.quest_desc: "\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"String Meshes are basic but useful. They're mainly used to sieve gravel for flint—essential for upgrading—or to sieve dirt for natural items like apricorns, for example."
	quest.6595523BFE3FDE67.quest_desc: "The incubator block increases the growth rate of baby villagers."
	quest.65E4A1A1B604B58B.quest_desc: "In time, you’ll come across a chest containing a few saplings. Don’t worry—you can always collect more as you go. This is just the beginning of your journey, so take your time and enjoy the process."
	quest.66EAB2AA7056CE07.quest_desc: "Like the name suggests — Simple Hats is all about funky little hats for your player to wear"
	quest.66EAB2AA7056CE07.title: "Hats"
	quest.69E0345D5A3BBA38.quest_desc: [
		"The villager item can be obtained by sneaking and right-clicking a villager or pressing the V (by default) key."
		""
		"The villager item can be placed by right-clicking on the ground."
		""
		"At least you won't have to find it behind a hill."
	]
	quest.6A740217E7F411AE.quest_desc: [
		"The three beasts of Johto never stop running."
		""
		"&7Only an absurd treasure makes one of them stop and look at you."
		""
		"&e&lIt will appear next to you.&r &7Do not let it flee."
	]
	quest.6A740217E7F411AE.quest_subtitle: "&7Legendary Beast"
	quest.6A740217E7F411AE.title: "&e&lRaikou"
	quest.6D32ABDFDBF57978.title: "Rare"
	quest.6D94B78D67EAAA1B.quest_desc: [
		"One of the three birds of Kanto."
		""
		"&7Gather enough to catch its attention. It will not be cheap."
		""
		"&e&lThe bird will appear next to you.&r &7Bring your best ball."
	]
	quest.6D94B78D67EAAA1B.quest_subtitle: "&7Legendary Bird"
	quest.6D94B78D67EAAA1B.title: "&b&lArticuno"
	quest.6DD1A38496B8FA68.quest_desc: [
		"Waystones are included in this pack to make travel easier between biomes, as they are still quite far apart.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\""
		""
		"Alternatively, if you'd like it to sound a bit more polished or formal:"
		""
		"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Waystones have been added to this pack to facilitate easier transportation between biomes, which are still widely separated."
	]
	quest.71AF2ECEAA04FF10.quest_desc: [
		"This compass will now help you locate biomes."
		"Why is that useful? Well, even in this one-block world, biomes still exist — they just don’t have any natural blocks where Cobblmon can spawn. That part’s up to you. But with this compass, you’ll at least know where to go."
	]
	quest.7258F09C57414BE1.quest_desc: [
		"&cNobody walks in here on luck.&r"
		""
		"Before dreaming of a legendary, show that you already mastered the"
		"basics: a full party, real wealth and experience to spare."
		""
		"&8This is only the gate. What comes after is worse."
	]
	quest.7258F09C57414BE1.quest_subtitle: "&7Prove you are worth it"
	quest.7258F09C57414BE1.title: "&6&lThe Call of Legends"
	quest.76A1B686E2D5E1CA.quest_desc: [
		"Cobblestone generators: put water and lava next to each other (with one empty block"
		"between them) and cobblestone appears where they meet, again and again."
		"Build one early: almost every recipe starts with cobblestone."
	]
	quest.7937585519D9159F.quest_desc: "You could eat them buttt....."
	quest.7AF5DECAEC4C8324.quest_desc: "This can be used to make lava soil. First, you’ll need a fire source—like a campfire, torch, or even some lava. Place cobblestone into the fire source and wait for the lava to form. Once it’s ready, you can use any kind of bucket to collect it."
	quest.7B25AFFD8C770A6C.quest_desc: "The auto trader works exactly like the trader block, except it automatically trades items for you. You can also automatically put items in and take items out with a hopper."
	quest.7DCFD0A363C2A834.quest_desc: [
		"Water + lava = cobblestone, forever."
		"Build a classic cobblestone generator on your island and collect &e64 Cobblestone&r."
		""
		"The next quests ask for the metals and gems you will dig out of the One Block."
	]
	quest.7DE4F3675B426C00.quest_desc: [
		"&d&lMythical Pokémon.&r"
		""
		"&7An independent trial. Four Master Balls is just the entry fee."
		""
		"&e&lIt will appear next to you.&r &7You still have to catch it."
	]
	quest.7DE4F3675B426C00.quest_subtitle: "&7Mythical"
	quest.7DE4F3675B426C00.title: "&d&lManaphy"
